From: tenstorrent.nix maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Support Blackhole packer zero-flag suppression in the dense data path

Applies to TTsim v1.10.6, a5276e15a52729465c8ddd71f0965df4ca2f0cc1.

Disable_pack_zero_flags controls output all-zero sideband metadata, not the
DstRowValid mask. The modeled Blackhole subset already writes every datum to
dense SRAM and performs near-memory accumulation on actual L1 data. Compression
and all sideband metadata consumers fail closed independently, so both values
are observationally equivalent within this supported subset. Keep the Wormhole
restriction and every unrelated unsupported guard unchanged. See the README
addition for immutable Blackhole-specific LLK and ISA authorities.

Focused behavioral regression lives beside this patch in
packer-zero-flags-regression.cpp; run-packer-zero-flags-regression.py compiles
and executes the actual model, not a copy of its arithmetic.

--- a/src/tensix.cpp
+++ b/src/tensix.cpp
@@ -2126,7 +2126,17 @@
 #endif
     PACK_VERIFY_THCON0(Exp_threshold_en);
     PACK_VERIFY_THCON0(Exp_threshold);
+#if TT_ARCH_VERSION == 0
     PACK_VERIFY_THCON0(Disable_pack_zero_flags);
+#else
+    // Blackhole Disable_pack_zero_flags controls output AllZeroFlags metadata, not DstRowValid
+    // (tt-llk tt_llk_blackhole/common/inc/cpack_common.h: reconfigure_packer_l1_acc).
+    // This model always materializes every output datum in dense SRAM, including zeroes from
+    // invalid Dst rows, then accumulates against the actual L1 datum when Pack_L1_Acc is set.
+    // Both flag values therefore have the same supported data-path semantics. Compression and
+    // all sideband metadata reads remain unsupported; do not infer metadata from pre-accumulate
+    // zeroes, or bypass read_dst16b/read_dst32b when the output metadata flag is disabled.
+#endif
 #undef PACK_VERIFY_THCON0
 
     uint32_t intermediate_format = p_config->ALU_FORMAT_SPEC_REG2_Dstacc;
