+### Local Blackhole packer data-path extension
+
+Both values of `THCON_SEC0_REG1_Disable_pack_zero_flags` are supported for the existing
+uncompressed Blackhole `PACR` data path. This is an output zero-metadata control, not the
+`DstRowValid` mask maintained by `ZEROACC`. The model materializes every datum in dense L1
+SRAM, including zeros from invalid Dst rows, and performs L1 accumulation on the actual L1
+value. Suppressing output zero metadata therefore needs no additional data-path state.
+In particular, packing a zero face during accumulation must not erase a nonzero L1 face.
+Dst contents, Dst validity, packer rounding, and accumulation arithmetic are unchanged.
+
+The Blackhole-specific control rationale is in
+[TT-Metal 0.77.0](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/tree/9f9cd4fd590f4b606bd0981a4fe0b6403eb38ec9),
+`tt_metal/tt-llk/tt_llk_blackhole/common/inc/cpack_common.h:333-342`, function
+`reconfigure_packer_l1_acc`: the zero flags describe the packer's outgoing face before
+the near-memory accumulation. In
+[the ISA contract](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-isa-documentation/tree/02d919f4c9c85ee23ce251b0e95c52300ec617d8),
+the Blackhole `Packers/README.md`, `TDMA-RISC.md`, and `SETDMAREG_Special.md` pages explicitly
+share their contracts with Wormhole; the latter two expose output zero flags as sideband metadata.
+This equivalence is restricted to the modeled data path: compression, sideband metadata
+reads (including tile headers), and Wormhole flag support remain unsupported. It does not
+implement or claim exact sideband zero-flag generation semantics.
+
